Build a self-contained Python 3 command-line script (Termux-style, shebang
pointing to `/data/data/com.termux/files/usr/bin/env python`) that converts HTML
files to Markdown.
Requirements: **Purpose:** Batch-convert `.html` and `.htm` files to `.md` files
using an external command-line converter named `rhtml2md`.
Each HTML file `name.html` (or `name.htm`) produces `name.md` in the same
directory, with the same stem.
Non-HTML files are ignored. **Dependencies:** - Use `from __future__ import
annotations` for type hints. - Standard library: `sys`, `pathlib.Path`. - Three
helpers imported from a local module named `dh`: - `get_files(directory)`:
returns an iterable of file paths found in a directory (assumed to recurse or
list files; treat as a black box). - `mpf(func, files)`: runs `func` over the
list of files, typically in parallel (multi-process/thread mapping); treat as a
black box. - `runcmd(argv_list, show_output=False)`: runs an external command
given as a list of arguments and returns a 3-tuple whose middle element is the
command's text output. **Inputs (command line):** - No arguments: process all
files returned by `get_files` on the current working directory. - One or more
arguments: each argument is a path.
If it is an existing file, add it to the work list.
If it is an existing directory, extend the work list with
`get_files(directory)`.
Paths that are neither are silently skipped. **Per-file processing
(`process_file(path)`):** - Convert the input to a `Path`. - Check the suffix
case-insensitively against `.html` and `.htm`.
For any other suffix, return `(path, False)` immediately without any work. - For
HTML files, compute the target as the same path with suffix changed to `.md`. -
Call `runcmd(["rhtml2md", str(path)], show_output=False)` and take the middle
element of the returned tuple as the Markdown text. - Write that text to the
target file with UTF-8 encoding. - On success, print `✓ Converted: <input
filename> -> <output filename>` to standard output and return `(md_file_path,
True)`. - On any exception, print `✗ Unexpected error converting <path>:
<error>` to standard error and return `(path, False)`.
Do not re-raise, so one failure does not stop the batch. **Main flow:** - Build
the file list as described above, then call `mpf(process_file, files)`.
The script does not itself collect or report the returned results. - Run
`main()` under the `if __name__ == "__main__":` guard, and exit via `raise
SystemExit(main())`, so the process exits with status 0 when `main` returns
`None`. **Edge cases to honor:** - Empty directories or directories with no
matching files produce no output and no error. - Arguments that do not exist are
silently ignored. - Uppercase extensions such as `.HTML` or `.Htm` are accepted.
- Non-HTML files passed explicitly are skipped without messages. - Encoding
errors in writing are caught by the general exception handler. - Output file
names are derived from the input stem, so an existing `.md` file with the same
stem will be overwritten. **Execution:** Run directly as an executable with the
Termux Python interpreter, or invoke with `python <script>` followed by optional
files or directories.
Requires the `rhtml2md` executable on PATH and the `dh` helper module importable
from the script's directory or the Python path. ---
